    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="8d1f861e-37cb-560d-be49-2dd4ad7efdc0" activityNameId="b602972c-3d43-52ef-81ec-af401abb02be" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Scantling, softwood, laminated, CFC, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Scantling, softwood, laminated, CFC, at plant
The thickness of the scantling is 0.071m. The bill of materials is based on data from two scantling producers. Allocation of co-products is either based on physical properties (wood inputs) or economical properties (working materials, production loss). An unweighted average was calculated.;
UUID: 29431bdb-ac29-310d-99bf-d1360ffca327
Included are the materials used in a laminated (C=continuous;F=finger-jointed) scantling. Production losses, work materials, packaging materials, energy demand and the transport of the materials are also included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at 2 scantling producers in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_29431bdb-ac29-310d-99bf-d1360ffca327.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
